<http://www.spektrix.com/tidemarktheatre/event/71401ARSRNJGNDQJKBJKRPKVJLLHLBTQD>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Donovan Woods";
  schema:description """
	What do Tim McGraw, Kenny Chesney, Charles Kelley of Lady A and the Barenaked Ladies have in common? They've all recorded songs written by Donovan Woods.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>And while his songs have found their way onto some pretty big stages, there's nothing quite like hearing them from the songwriter himself.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>With his clever observations, dry humour and knack for saying the things most people are thinking but rarely say out loud, Donovan Woods has built a career making music that's as relatable as it is memorable. His songs move effortlessly between folk, country and pop, tackling everything from complicated relationships to life's unexpected turns.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>His latest album, <span class=\"ItalicText\">Things Were Never Good If They're Not Good Now</span>, earned a spot on the Polaris Music Prize longlist, while his 2026 EP, <span class=\"ItalicText\">Squander Your Gifts</span>, offers five new songs inspired by the life and loss of his close friend and songwriting partner, Abe Stoklasa.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>On February 9, 2027, Donovan Woods brings his music to the Tidemark Theatre for a night of great songs, clever storytelling and plenty of personality.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Tickets: $40 Members, $45 Non-Members <span class=\"ItalicText\">(+applicable taxes & fees)</span>
""";
  schema:startDate "2027-02-09T19:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/tidemarktheatre/files/5f363ba2-dc96-4718-bb7a-32df552f33d7.jpg>;
