<http://www.spektrix.com/tidemarktheatre/event/68801ALBSQSHRCDRCGNPHHPCVVCPMPMDD>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Kathleen Edwards";
  schema:description """
	With more than two decades of acclaimed songwriting, Kathleen Edwards has established herself as one of Canada's leading voices in alt-country and roots music.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Since her 2002 debut <span class=\"ItalicText\">Failer</span>, the Ottawa-born singer-songwriter has earned more than half a dozen JUNO Award nominations, chart success on both sides of the border and a devoted following drawn to her honest lyrics, memorable melodies and guitar-driven sound.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>She's shared stages with Willie Nelson, Bob Dylan and John Fogerty, collaborated with Maren Morris, and even stepped away from music for a few years to open a coffee shop called <span class=\"ItalicText\">Quitters</span>. Thankfully, she didn't stay away for good.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>With a sound that draws from folk, country and rock & roll, Edwards continues to write and perform on her own terms, bringing together the storytelling and musicianship that have made her a favourite among fans and fellow artists.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Great songs, great stories and a little rock & roll. Kathleen Edwards brings it all to the Tidemark Theatre on March 14, 2027.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Tickets: $48 Members, $53 Non-Members <span class=\"ItalicText\">(+applicable taxes & fees)</span>
""";
  schema:startDate "2027-03-14T19:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/tidemarktheatre/files/56b16a40-abbf-4f78-8d5f-708fdc84836b.jpg>;
  schema:location <https://spektrix.com/tidemarktheatre/location/405AGDKDKNLGVLJCSNTLQBVTRTGBTHCPJ>;
