<http://www.spektrix.com/tidemarktheatre/event/67201AVCRKQDBSGLQHRCLJQTBDLCTLNNQ>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Matt Andersen";
  schema:description """
	Matt Andersen has spent more than two decades earning a reputation as one of Canada’s great live performers, bringing his unmistakable voice and incredible guitar playing to stages around the world.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>From intimate theatres to major international festivals, the New Brunswick singer-songwriter has built a devoted following with performances that can shift from quiet and soulful to big and powerful. He’s toured and shared stages with Marcus King, Beth Hart, Gregg Allman, Tedeschi Trucks Band, Randy Bachman, Serena Ryder, and more.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Andersen was the first Canadian to win the solo category at the International Blues Challenge in Memphis, has earned multiple Maple Blues Awards and two European Blues Awards, and received a 2024 JUNO nomination with <span class=\"ItalicText\">Matt Andersen & The Big Bottle of Joy</span>.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Now touring in support of his latest album, <span class=\"ItalicText\">The Hammer & The Rose</span>, Andersen returns to the Tidemark after selling out the theatre on his last visit.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>If you’ve seen Matt Andersen before, you already know. If you haven’t, this is your chance.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Opening the show is Canadian singer-songwriter Dave Sampson, whose powerful voice, catchy folk-pop melodies and high-energy performances have been winning over audiences across the country. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Dave has collaborated with artists including Alan Doyle, Donovan Woods and Classified, and worked with Grammy Award-winning producer Gordie Sampson. Selected for Canada's Walk of Fame Emerging Artist Program, Dave continues to make his mark as one of Canada's exciting emerging songwriters.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Tickets: $57 Admission <span class=\"ItalicText\">(+applicable taxes & fees)</span>
""";
  schema:startDate "2027-03-13T19:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/tidemarktheatre/files/a5f4ff62-86b0-4684-b8e0-3e345955e20a.jpg>;
