<http://www.spektrix.com/tidemarktheatre/event/66601AGQCGDBVSBRBPDBPSKRTDHMKTVRL>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Shaun Majumder";
  schema:description """
	Shaun Majumder is an award-winning actor, comedian, writer, producer, and director whose career has spanned more than two decades across television, film, and live performance.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>He currently stars as “Father Khatri” in MGM+‘s acclaimed series FROM and recently appeared as “Gary” in Peacock’s The Miniature Wife, opposite Elizabeth Banks and Matthew Macfadyen. His recent work also includes portraying “Dr. Voor” in Star Trek: Strange New Worlds. Equally adept in comedy and drama, Shaun’s screen credits include 24, The Firm, Detroit 1-8-7, Unhitched, and Cedric the Entertainer Presents.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Shaun first became a household name through his legendary seventeen-season run on CBC’s This Hour Has 22 Minutes, where his singular voice as a performer and writer earned multiple Gemini and Canadian Screen Awards, establishing him as one of Canada’s most distinctive comedic talents.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Today, Shaun’s creative focus is increasingly centered on authorship and original storytelling through his production company, LAFBOY. Conceived as a home for bold, emotionally resonant stories, LAFBOY is dedicated to creating work that moves people. Projects that balance humour and heart while exploring identity, family, belonging, and the complexities of human connection.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>As a writer, producer, and director, Shaun is developing a slate of premium film and television projects that reflect his unique perspective and genre-fluid sensibility, ranging from elevated comedy and prestige drama to socially conscious storytelling rooted in character and place.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>With a career that continues to evolve beyond performance alone, Shaun Majumder is emerging as a singular creative voice, committed to building meaningful, globally relevant stories that entertain, challenge, and endure.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Tickets: $54 Admission <span class=\"ItalicText\">(+applicable taxes & fees)</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\"><span class=\"BoldText\">Content Warning: 19+ Event</span></span>
""";
  schema:startDate "2027-01-18T19:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/tidemarktheatre/files/13b892b6-3a22-472b-a8b1-2bf135e87f7e.jpg>;
